    {
      "page_title": "switch and restore",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "number": 1,
          "title": "switch and restore",
          "tagline": "one verb per intent"
        },
        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "git",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "switch moves between branches; restore fixes files. Both arrived in Git 2.23."
            },
            {
              "icon": "lightbulb",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "checkout did two jobs; 'checkout foo' was ambiguous, typos lost work."
            },
            {
              "icon": "zap",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "switch moves or creates branches; restore discards edits or unstages."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How it works",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Touches",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`git switch -c fix/login origin/main`",
              "HEAD",
              "new branch off main"
            ],
            [
              "`git restore src/a.js`",
              "working tree",
              "unstaged edits gone"
            ],
            [
              "`git restore --staged src/a.js`",
              "index",
              "unstaged, edits kept"
            ],
            [
              "`git restore --source=HEAD~2 src/a.js`",
              "working tree",
              "file from 2 commits ago"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One verb per intent, so no ambiguous ==checkout==",
            "`restore --staged` replaces cryptic `reset HEAD file`",
            "`switch` refuses to clobber a dirty tree",
            "`--source` reads any commit's version of a file"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`restore file` **permanently** drops edits, not in reflog",
            "`switch -c` without a start point uses HEAD",
            "`--detach` leaves you on a detached HEAD"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Interview takeaway:",
          "text": "switch moves HEAD, restore rewrites files, and neither rewrites history.\n`restore --staged` only unstages, while plain `restore` destroys unstaged work."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "aside": "Split from checkout"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "stash",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "number": 2,
          "title": "git stash",
          "tagline": "park it, don't commit it"
        },
        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "layers",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "Shelves uncommitted changes on a stack; clean HEAD"
            },
            {
              "icon": "lightbulb",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "Switching or pulling needs a clean tree"
            },
            {
              "icon": "zap",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "Hotfixes, dirty pulls, moving half-done work"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How it works",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Effect",
            "Stack after"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`stash push -m \"wip: cart total\"`",
              "saves tracked",
              "`stash@{0}`"
            ],
            [
              "`stash list`",
              "shows stack",
              "`stash@{0}: wip: cart total`"
            ],
            [
              "`stash pop`",
              "applies, **drops**",
              "empty"
            ],
            [
              "`stash apply stash@{1}`",
              "applies, **keeps**",
              "unchanged"
            ],
            [
              "`refs/stash`",
              "merge commits",
              "newest on top"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Instant clean tree, one command",
            "`-u` includes untracked files",
            "`-p` stashes chosen hunks",
            "`git stash branch fix-cart` makes a branch"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Untracked, ignored skipped without `-u`/`-a`",
            "`pop` on conflict **keeps** the stash",
            "Easy to forget: name with `-m`",
            "Local only, never pushed"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Interview takeaway:",
          "text": "Stash is a ==stack of temporary commits==, not a backup; prefer **apply** over pop.\nLong-lived work belongs on a WIP branch."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "aside": "a stack, not backup",
      "subtitle": "Shelve work, keep HEAD clean"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Reading History",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "number": 3,
          "title": "log --graph and blame -w"
        },
        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "git",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "--graph draws the commit DAG; blame -w skips whitespace edits"
            },
            {
              "icon": "lightbulb",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "History is a graph, and a reformat hides a line's real author"
            },
            {
              "icon": "search",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "Merge topology, why a line exists, tracing code authorship"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How it works",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`git log --graph --oneline --decorate --all`",
              "every branch drawn, labelled"
            ],
            [
              "`git blame -w -L 40,60 src/pay.js`",
              "lines 40-60, whitespace skipped"
            ],
            [
              "`git blame -w -M -C src/pay.js`",
              "follows moved or copied lines"
            ],
            [
              "`git log -L 40,60:src/pay.js`",
              "every change to those lines"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Graph exposes ==diverged branches== and merge points at a glance",
            "`-w` stops an indent-only commit from stealing credit",
            "`-L` limits output to just the lines you care about"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Blame shows the **last** touch, not the origin: follow with `log -L`",
            "Bulk reformat: use `--ignore-rev` or `.git-blame-ignore-revs`",
            "Graph is unreadable on huge repos without `--first-parent`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Interview takeaway:",
          "text": "`blame` answers ==who last changed== a line; `log -S/-L` answers when it appeared.\nUse `-w -M -C` to see past cosmetic edits and refactor moves."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "aside": "who touched it?",
      "subtitle": "log --graph, blame -w"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "cherry-pick",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "number": 4,
          "title": "cherry-pick",
          "tagline": "one fix, no merge"
        },
        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "git",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "Copies one commit's change onto the current branch as a new commit."
            },
            {
              "icon": "lightbulb",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "Take one fix without merging the whole branch it lives on."
            },
            {
              "icon": "zap",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "Backport hotfix to release/1.4, rescue abandoned commits, borrow teammate's fix."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How it works",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "tables",
          "spec": {
            "tables": [
              {
                "title": "main",
                "headers": [
                  "SHA",
                  "Message"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "c9d8e7f",
                    "add search"
                  ],
                  [
                    "a1b2c3d",
                    "fix null token"
                  ],
                  [
                    "3b4a5c6",
                    "tweak css"
                  ]
                ],
                "caption": "a1b2c3d diffed against its parent"
              },
              {
                "title": "release/1.4: cherry-pick -x a1b2c3d",
                "headers": [
                  "New SHA",
                  "Message"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "8e7f6a5",
                    "bump 1.4.2"
                  ],
                  [
                    "5d4c3b2",
                    "fix null token + -x note"
                  ]
                ],
                "caption": "Same message, new SHA. Range: A^..B"
              }
            ],
            "arrow": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Surgical: one change, **no merge noise**",
            "`-x` adds `(cherry picked from a1b2c3d)` audit trail",
            "`-n` applies the change without committing",
            "`-m 1` picks a merge relative to its first parent"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "New SHA: merging both branches later can **conflict** or duplicate",
            "Conflict? Fix files, then `--continue` or `--abort`",
            "Picking a merge fails without `-m`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Interview takeaway:",
          "text": "Cherry-pick replays a **diff**, not a commit: the result is a different commit.\nUse it for backports; prefer merge or rebase for normal integration."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "aside": "copy, not move!",
      "subtitle": "Copy one commit"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "worktree",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "number": 5,
          "title": "git worktree",
          "tagline": "two branches, live at once"
        },
        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "folder",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "Extra working folders sharing one .git, each on its own branch"
            },
            {
              "icon": "lightbulb",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "Stash interrupts your flow; a second clone duplicates all history"
            },
            {
              "icon": "git",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "PR review, long tests on one branch, parallel agent sessions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How it works",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "What happens"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`git worktree add ../app-hotfix -b hotfix/401 origin/main`",
              "new folder, new branch; commit there"
            ],
            [
              "`git worktree list`",
              "shows every tree; metadata in .git/worktrees/"
            ],
            [
              "`git worktree remove ../app-hotfix`",
              "deletes folder and its metadata"
            ],
            [
              "`git worktree prune`",
              "clears entries for vanished folders"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{icon:check} No **stashing**: your work stays untouched",
            "Shared objects: cheap disk use, ==instant fetches==",
            "Separate build dirs and files per branch"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A branch is checked out in **one** worktree only",
            "Each tree needs its own `node_modules` or venv",
            "Delete with `remove` or `prune`, never just `rm -rf`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Interview takeaway:",
          "text": "Worktrees give parallel checkouts from a single repo.\nReach for them over stash or a second clone when two branches must be live."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "aside": "one repo, many folders",
      "subtitle": "Parallel checkouts"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "rebase -i",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "number": 6,
          "title": "git rebase -i",
          "tagline": "edit the plan"
        },
        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "git",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "Replays commits onto a base while you **edit the plan**."
            },
            {
              "icon": "lightbulb",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "First drafts are messy; reviewers want a clean, logical sequence."
            },
            {
              "icon": "zap",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "Squash WIP, reword, split big commits, drop debug commits."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How it works",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "tables",
          "spec": {
            "tables": [
              {
                "title": "git rebase -i HEAD~4",
                "headers": [
                  "Cmd",
                  "Commit"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "a1b2c3d add cart"
                  ],
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "e4f5a6b wip"
                  ],
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "9c8d7e6 fix typo"
                  ],
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "5d4c3b2 add tests"
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Edit 2nd + 3rd",
                "headers": [
                  "Cmd",
                  "Commit"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "a1b2c3d add cart"
                  ],
                  [
                    "fixup",
                    "e4f5a6b wip"
                  ],
                  [
                    "fixup",
                    "9c8d7e6 fix typo"
                  ],
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "5d4c3b2 add tests"
                  ]
                ],
                "caption": "pick, reword, edit, squash, fixup, drop"
              },
              {
                "title": "Result",
                "headers": [
                  "New SHA",
                  "Message"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "7f1e2a9",
                    "add cart"
                  ],
                  [
                    "c3b8d40",
                    "add tests"
                  ]
                ],
                "caption": "4 commits become 2"
              }
            ],
            "arrow": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**Benefits:** readable, ==bisectable== history",
            "Fixes mistakes before anyone else sees them",
            "`--onto` moves a branch to a new base",
            "`--abort` restores the original state"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**Consider:** it rewrites SHAs, so never rebase commits others pulled",
            "After a push, use `git push --force-with-lease`, never plain `--force`",
            "Conflicts may repeat per commit; `rerere` helps"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Interview takeaway:",
          "text": "rebase -i rewrites history by creating **new commits**: free on private branches, never on shared ones. Force-push only with `--force-with-lease`."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "aside": "private branches only",
      "subtitle": "Rewrite history cleanly"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "commit --fixup and autosquash",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "number": 7,
          "title": "commit --fixup + autosquash"
        },
        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "git",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "`--fixup <sha>` marks a fix; ==autosquash== folds it into its target"
            },
            {
              "icon": "lightbulb",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "Fix an earlier commit mid-feature without hand-editing the rebase todo"
            },
            {
              "icon": "github",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "Applying review feedback to the right commit; clean PR series"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How it works",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "tables",
          "spec": {
            "tables": [
              {
                "title": "git commit --fixup 3f2a1bc",
                "headers": [
                  "sha",
                  "subject"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "3f2a1bc",
                    "add cart total"
                  ],
                  [
                    "8d4e9f1",
                    "add coupon"
                  ],
                  [
                    "c7b6a05",
                    "fixup! add cart total"
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "rebase -i --autosquash origin/main",
                "headers": [
                  "action",
                  "subject"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "add cart total"
                  ],
                  [
                    "**fixup**",
                    "fixup! add cart total"
                  ],
                  [
                    "pick",
                    "add coupon"
                  ]
                ],
                "caption": "save and exit: done"
              }
            ],
            "arrow": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==No manual== todo editing: just save and exit",
            "`git config rebase.autoSquash true` makes it the default",
            "`--squash!` variant also lets you edit the message",
            "`--fixup=amend:<sha>` rewrites the message"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Target must be __inside the rebase range__",
            "Still **rewrites history**: same shared-branch rule as rebase -i",
            "Find the sha: `git log --oneline` or `git absorb`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Interview takeaway:",
          "text": "Fixup commit = marker + autosquash: fix an old commit without opening the todo list.\nSet `rebase.autoSquash` to true."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "aside": "fix it, don't fumble"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "reflog",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "number": 8,
          "title": "reflog",
          "tagline": "nothing is lost yet"
        },
        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "git",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "Local log of every position HEAD and branch tips have held"
            },
            {
              "icon": "lightbulb",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "Unreachable commits look lost, but Git keeps them for a while"
            },
            {
              "icon": "zap",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "Undo bad reset or rebase, recover deleted branches, find yesterday's HEAD"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How it works",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Step",
            "Command",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1. Oops",
              "`git reset --hard HEAD~3`",
              "3 commits vanish"
            ],
            [
              "2. Look",
              "`git reflog`",
              "`e4f5a6b HEAD@{1}: commit: add cart`"
            ],
            [
              "3. Restore",
              "`git reset --hard e4f5a6b`",
              "branch is back"
            ],
            [
              "4. Or copy",
              "`git branch rescue e4f5a6b`",
              "safe branch, no reset"
            ],
            [
              "5. By time",
              "`main@{2.days.ago}`",
              "main as of 2 days ago"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Safety net for nearly every history mistake",
            "Per-branch logs, like `main@{2.days.ago}`",
            "Works with any ref syntax, e.g. `HEAD@{n}`"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Local only: **never** pushed or cloned",
            "Entries expire after 90 days (30 if unreachable), then gc prunes",
            "Uncommitted changes were never recorded, so **unrecoverable**"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Interview takeaway:",
          "text": "reflog is the undo history for refs.\n==Committed once== means recoverable; **never committed** means gone."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "aside": "your undo button",
      "subtitle": "the undo history"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "bisect",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "number": 9,
          "title": "bisect",
          "tagline": "halve the history"
        },
        {
          "type": "labelrows",
          "rows": [
            {
              "icon": "git",
              "label": "What it is:",
              "text": "Binary-searches commit history to find the exact commit that introduced a bug."
            },
            {
              "icon": "lightbulb",
              "label": "Why it exists:",
              "text": "Hundreds of commits make checking each one by hand slow."
            },
            {
              "icon": "zap",
              "label": "Used for:",
              "text": "Pinpointing regressions; automating the hunt with a test script."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How it works",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git bisect start",
            "git bisect bad            # HEAD broken",
            "git bisect good v2.3      # works",
            "# 128 commits: ~7 steps (log2 128)",
            "git bisect reset          # finish"
          ],
          "note": "mark each checkout good or bad",
          "result": {
            "headers": [
              "Step",
              "Tested",
              "Verdict"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "1",
                "#64",
                "bad"
              ],
              [
                "2",
                "#32",
                "good"
              ],
              [
                "3",
                "#48",
                "bad"
              ],
              [
                "7",
                "#37",
                "first bad"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{green:O(log n)} steps: 128 commits need about 7",
            "`git bisect run npm test` goes fully hands-free",
            "`git bisect skip` passes untestable commits",
            "bisect log can be replayed"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Needs a reliable good/bad test",
            "Exit code **125** tells run to skip",
            "Good commit must be a true ancestor",
            "Merge-heavy history is fuzzy: use `--first-parent`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "solid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Interview takeaway:",
          "text": "bisect finds the first bad commit in log2(n) steps, and 'bisect run' with a script makes it hands-free.\nSmall, atomic commits make the answer exact."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "aside": "think binary!",
      "subtitle": "Hunt the bad commit"
