  "caption": {
    "text": "Most devs stop at add, commit, push. Then they freeze when an interviewer asks how they'd recover a lost commit or find the change that broke prod. These 10 Git concepts are what seniors reach for every day.\n\n1. switch and restore\n2. stash\n3. Reading History: log --graph and blame -w\n4. cherry-pick\n5. worktree\n6. rebase -i\n7. commit --fixup and autosquash\n8. reflog\n9. bisect\n10. range-diff\n\nEach one covers what it is, why it exists, a worked example, the trade-offs and the interview takeaway. The last slide is a cheatsheet of all 12 commands.\n\nWhich one confuses you most? Tell me below 👇\n\nComment “git” and save this for your next interview.",
